WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.063
My name is Maya Greyy,

00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:10.871
and I have a YouTube channel

00:00:10.871 --> 00:00:12.745
where I express my creativity

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.390
and show the love for my dolls.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.030
I'm going to be walking you guys through

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.060
on how I restored this
Bratz Campfire Felicia doll.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.370
Felicia is from the Campfire line

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.250
that Bratz released in 2005.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.183
Even though she was very underrated

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:30.624
when she first came
out, she quickly became

00:00:30.624 --> 00:00:33.729
one of the most sought-after
dolls to this day.

00:00:33.729 --> 00:00:36.550
Felicia pretty much came
with her full outfit.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.116
She came with a haircut,

00:00:38.116 --> 00:00:41.382
a missing left brow, and lip chips.

00:00:41.382 --> 00:00:44.240
And she also came with marks on her body,

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.490
which looked like pens or like crayons.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.450
I'm going to be undressing the doll

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.150
just to make it easier for me

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.100
and just to wash the clothes as well,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.760
since they came very dirty.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.220
I'm going to be taking her head off,

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.870
which is going to help
me with cutting her hair,

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.630
removing what's inside as well.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.590
Her hair came very chopped.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:13.980
It was cut short.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.021
I'm just going to be using some scissors

00:01:16.021 --> 00:01:17.496
to cut her hair.

00:01:17.496 --> 00:01:18.890
And you want to make sure

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.160
that you're cutting down to the roots,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.960
pretty much just to get rid of it

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.653
and have a clean slate
for the new rerooted hair.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.602
I'm going to be putting her hair

00:01:31.602 --> 00:01:33.277
into boiling-hot water,

00:01:33.277 --> 00:01:35.860
and this will soften up her vinyl,

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.340
like the plastic, the head,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.330
to make it easier for you
to pluck the hair out.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.733
And it also does soften
the glue inside the head.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.280
I'm going to be using pointy tweezers

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.020
to pretty much pick out the remaining hair

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.330
that's inside the head,

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:55.090
just to make it cleaner
and easier for the reroot,

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.920
and there's no remaining hair

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.253
that's going to be poking
out with all of her new hair.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.458
Rerooting is pretty much replacing

00:02:07.458 --> 00:02:10.540
all of her hair that's already rooted.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.400
I'm going to be using saran hair,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.843
which is pretty much the same

00:02:13.843 --> 00:02:16.540
as her factory hair that she came with.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:18.180
And I also picked out

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.250
the most similar colors that I could find,

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.220
just to match it all exactly.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.750
So, using a rerooting tool,

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.940
I'm going to be poking
each hair into the head

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.163
pretty much exactly how
they did it in the factory.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:36.700
I used the base of an
X-Acto knife, a needle,

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.330
and I have a pick to help
me poke holes into the doll

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.280
just to make it easier for the needle.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.750
And it will also save you some needles,

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.670
because it will break if
the hole isn't big enough

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.710
or the plastic has hardened.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.350
So, starting off with the reroot,

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.150
I just sectioned out some hair

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.090
to make it easier for me.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.181
Each strand of hair I pretty much

00:02:57.181 --> 00:02:59.039
wrap around my finger.

00:02:59.039 --> 00:03:01.660
I use that to guide the needle

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.390
and guide the hair into the needle.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.090
I use my pick to create a bigger hole

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.700
into the doll's head,

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.600
and then after that I
use my rerooting tool

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.553
to insert the hair into the doll's head.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.637
Some of the existing
holes might be already

00:03:18.637 --> 00:03:20.660
too big or already cracked.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:24.130
So if you're using a pick
to widen up the holes,

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.748
just be careful just in case

00:03:25.748 --> 00:03:28.240
you might crack a big hole into her head

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.423
or crack the plastic even more.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.823
So, the doll came with some pen marks

00:03:35.823 --> 00:03:37.414
all over her body.

00:03:37.414 --> 00:03:39.340
I'm going to be using some alcohol,

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:42.048
since it kind of stained the plastic.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.420
She came with chipped
brows and chipped lips,

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.300
so I'm just going to be repainting them

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.092
using some acrylic paint

00:03:57.092 --> 00:03:59.959
and some nail polish that I have.

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:02.010
I just use a normal paintbrush

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.060
typically used for doll repaints.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.060
And these are usually smaller
than normal paintbrushes,

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.660
since it's for detailing.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.618
During repainting, it's important

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.800
to have a steady hand.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.800
If there's any mistakes

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.900
that I've done with the repainting,

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.280
I'm going to be using some rubbing alcohol

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.580
just to remove some of the imperfections

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.900
or just to clean up the
repainting just a little bit,

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.553
just to make her eyebrow more sharp.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.140
So, with repainting her lips,

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:36.940
I used nail polish that
was pretty much clear,

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.455
and I used some eye shadow

00:04:38.455 --> 00:04:40.305
that was pretty similar

00:04:40.305 --> 00:04:42.213
to her lip color that I found.

00:04:42.213 --> 00:04:43.530
So it was pretty lucky.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.730
So I just mixed the clear nail polish

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.130
and the eye shadow together

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:50.130
just to have a paint consistency,

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:53.717
and I just used that to repaint her lips.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.847
I pretty much just used a normal

00:05:01.847 --> 00:05:04.320
washing detergent for her clothes

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.820
and used it with some lukewarm water.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.361
So I pretty much just kind of

00:05:08.361 --> 00:05:09.694
scrunch it up in the water,

00:05:09.694 --> 00:05:12.770
just making sure all
the dirt is out of it.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.156
You can see by the water

00:05:20.156 --> 00:05:22.089
how dirty the clothes came in.

00:05:22.089 --> 00:05:25.393
So it was definitely a
good decision to wash them.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.598
I'm going to be redressing her

00:05:30.598 --> 00:05:32.783
back into the clothes that she came with.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.701
They are the original clothes

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.384
from the Campfire line,

00:05:38.384 --> 00:05:40.458
just some pieces missing.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.650
I am very happy with this restoration,

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:52.060
and I'm happy to have Felicia
in my doll collection,

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.500
since she is very sought after

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.633
and very loved by a lot of collectors.

